## Memory Management

### Cleanup Socket & Timer Effects
Music-room sync and presence rely on long-lived socket connections and
recurring timers (the NTP-style re-sync every 30s per [[08-music-rooms]]) —
these must be torn down on unmount or they'll keep firing against a
component that's no longer there:

```javascript
// ✅ Correct - Cleanup subscriptions and timers
import React, { useEffect, useRef } from 'react'

const useRoomSync = (roomId, socket) => {
  const syncIntervalRef = useRef(null)

  useEffect(() => {
    const requestSync = () => {
      socket.emit('room:sync_request', { t1: Date.now() })
    }

    requestSync()
    syncIntervalRef.current = setInterval(requestSync, 30000)

    return () => {
      // Cleanup interval on unmount / roomId change
      if (syncIntervalRef.current) {
        clearInterval(syncIntervalRef.current)
      }
    }
  }, [roomId, socket])
}
```

### Avoid Memory Leaks — Abort In-Flight Requests
```javascript
// ✅ Correct - Cancel ongoing requests
import React, { useEffect, useRef } from 'react'

const MessageSearch = ({ query }) => {
  const abortControllerRef = useRef(null)

  useEffect(() => {
    abortControllerRef.current = new AbortController()

    const search = async () => {
      try {
        const response = await fetch(`/api/messages/search?q=${query}`, {
          signal: abortControllerRef.current.signal
        })
        const data = await response.json()
        setResults(data)
      } catch (error) {
        if (error.name !== 'AbortError') {
          console.error('Search failed:', error)
        }
      }
    }

    search()

    return () => {
      if (abortControllerRef.current) {
        abortControllerRef.current.abort()
      }
    }
  }, [query])

  return <div>Search results...</div>
}
```

## Image & Media Optimization

### Lazy Loading Avatars/Story Thumbnails
```javascript
// src/components/common/LazyImageComponent.jsx
import React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from 'react'
import { Box, Skeleton } from '@mui/material'

const LazyImageComponent = ({ src, alt, ...props }) => {
  const [isLoaded, setIsLoaded] = useState(false)
  const [isInView, setIsInView] = useState(false)
  const imgRef = useRef(null)

  useEffect(() => {
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
      ([entry]) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          setIsInView(true)
          observer.disconnect()
        }
      },
      { threshold: 0.1 }
    )

    if (imgRef.current) {
      observer.observe(imgRef.current)
    }

    return () => observer.disconnect()
  }, [])

  return (
    <Box ref={imgRef} {...props}>
      {isInView && (
        <img
          src={src}
          alt={alt}
          onLoad={() => setIsLoaded(true)}
          style={{ display: isLoaded ? 'block' : 'none' }}
        />
      )}
      {!isLoaded && <Skeleton variant="rectangular" width="100%" height="200px" />}
    </Box>
  )
}

export default LazyImageComponent
```

## Performance Monitoring

### React DevTools Profiler
```javascript
// Wrap expensive components with Profiler
import React, { Profiler } from 'react'

const onRenderCallback = (id, phase, actualDuration) => {
  console.log('Component:', id, 'Phase:', phase, 'Duration:', actualDuration)
}

const App = () => {
  return (
    <Profiler id="App" onRender={onRenderCallback}>
      <Router>
        <Routes>
          <Route path="/conversations" element={<ConversationsPage />} />
        </Routes>
      </Router>
    </Profiler>
  )
}
```

### Performance Metrics
```javascript
// src/utils/performance.utils.js
export const measurePerformance = (name, fn) => {
  const start = performance.now()
  const result = fn()
  const end = performance.now()

  console.log(`${name} took ${end - start} milliseconds`)
  return result
}

// Usage
const computeQueueStats = (queue) => {
  return measurePerformance('Queue Stats Calculation', () => {
    return calculateQueueStats(queue)
  })
}
```

## Mobile Performance

### Touch Optimization
```javascript
// src/components/mui/TouchOptimizedButtonComponent.jsx
import React, { memo } from 'react'
import { Button } from '@mui/material'

const TouchOptimizedButtonComponent = memo(({ children, ...props }) => {
  return (
    <Button
      {...props}
      sx={{
        minHeight: 44, // Minimum touch target size
        minWidth: 44,
        touchAction: 'manipulation', // Disable double-tap zoom
        ...props.sx
      }}
    >
      {children}
    </Button>
  )
})

export default TouchOptimizedButtonComponent
```

### Reduce Motion for Accessibility
```javascript
// src/utils/accessibility.utils.js
export const prefersReducedMotion = () => {
  return window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches
}

// Usage in animations
const AnimatedComponent = () => {
  const shouldAnimate = !prefersReducedMotion()

  return (
    <div style={{ transition: shouldAnimate ? 'transform 0.3s ease' : 'none' }}>
      Content
    </div>
  )
}
```
